; The lowercase half of 495, and the half that was silent.
;
; `Double` and `U8` next door draw AX3002 because they are
; CAPITALISED: an unknown uppercase name is an unknown type
; CONSTRUCTOR, and the checker resolves it and fails. A lowercase name
; in type position is a type VARIABLE, and there is no such thing as
; an unknown one - so `u64` did not fail, it SUCCEEDED, binding a
; fresh variable and generalising the signature over it.
;
; Measured on 0.3.1, which is why this is an error rather than a
; lint: with the body below and `(f "not a number")` at the call
; site, `axiom check` printed OK, `axiom run` exited 0, and the
; program ran. `(:: f (-> u64 Int))` means `forall n. n -> Int`, which
; is the OPPOSITE of the constraint the spelling looks like.
;
; This is `.axbad` because the refusal is at parse time, so the file
; does not parse and `check-fmt`/`check-tree-sitter` must not sweep it
; as source.
(:: f (-> u64 Int))

(fn (f x) 7)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (f 41))
